

**PROBABILITY FUNCTIONS**

**Relation of the Characteristic Function to Moments About the Origin**

\(26.1.11\)\(\phi^{(n)}(0)\!=\!\left[\frac{d^{n}}{dt^{n}}\phi(t)\right]_{t=0}\!=\!i^{n}\mu _{n}^{\prime}\)

**Cumulant Function**

\(26.1.12\)\(\ln\,\phi(t)\!=\!\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\kappa_{n}\frac{(it)^{n}}{n!}\)

\(\kappa_{n}\) is called the \(n^{\rm th}\) cumulant.

\(26.1.13\)\(\kappa_{1}\!=\!m\), \(\kappa_{1}\!=\!\sigma^{2}\), \(\kappa_{3}\!=\!\mu_{j}\), \(\kappa_{4}\!=\!\mu_{4}\!-\!3\mu_{2}^{2}\)

**Relation of Central Moments to Moments About the Origin**

\(26.1.14\)\(\mu_{n}\!=\!\sum\limits_{j=0}^{n}\binom{n}{j}(-1)^{n-j}\mu_{j}^{\prime}m^{ n-j}\)